-- title:
--   Equal branch values at a supersingular node, q<5
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q<5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$), let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$, and suppose $a^{q^2}=a$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series. Assume: $f$, viewed as a Laurent series, is integral over the subring `NodeLocalized.modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A.toSubring red a (a ^ q)` of Laurent series annihilated-by-denominator at the point $(a,a^q)$, namely those $g$ with $g\cdot\mathrm{modularEval}(s)=\mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ for some two-variable polynomials $r,s$ over $A$ with $\mathrm{pointEval}(s)(a,a^q)\neq 0$; and that both $f$ and its image under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with $j(q_\tau)$ and $j(q_\tau^{\,1\cdot q})$ at the complement of the kernel of reduction, with reductions under `modularRedLocHom` lying in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated over $k$ by $j(q_\tau)$ and $j(q_\tau^{\,1})$. Then there exists $c\in k$ such that both places of the pair `frobNodePair q a`, namely the geometric places attached to the points $a$ and $a^q$ of the $j$-line over $k$, take the value $c$: the first at the reduction of $f$ and the second at the reduction of the Fricke image of $f$, where having value $c$ means the element lies in the valuation subring of the place and its residue is the image of $c$ in the residue field.
--
--   This is the small-characteristic half ($q<5$) of the statement that a function integral over the local ring of a supersingular node takes the same value on the two branches meeting there, the two branches being indexed by the Frobenius-conjugate points $a$ and $a^q$ of the $j$-line. It is combined with the complementary case through [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_degenerate`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_degenerate), en route to the description of the mod $q$ fibre of the modular curve of level $q$ used in level lowering.
